      "summary": {
        "text": "Animated multispectral satellite imagery (MSI) depicts tropical storm (TS) 26W (choi-wan) improving in structure with a more symmetrical and partially obscured low level circulation center (LLCC). TS 26W has slowed in track speed and begun a poleward turn as it enters an area of weaker steering influence as a shortwave trough to the north propagates eastward, weakening the western extension of the subtropical ridge (STR) centered to the northeast. Regarding intensity, 26W is forecast to continue intensifying out to a peak of 105 kt between taus 48 and 60, with a period of rapid intensification (ri) explicitly forecast from +12h to 36 as 26W gains a poleward outflow channel and VWS continues to abate.",
